      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of being an empty shell is the most honest description of what it feels like when your anchor is gone. Trying to \"fill\" a void like this is a monumental, impossible task, so don't put that pressure on yourself. Instead, consider the gentle, quiet act of simply letting yourself be taken care of by the outside world—a small, deliberate act of self-kindness, like a slow, deep breath. You don't have to find a grand purpose right now; just focus on surviving the next hour.",
